*  PUSH_driver - exercises PUSH(X)/POP()/TOP() over the stack in PUSH_POP.
*  Contract per PUSH.sno header: PUSH returns BY NAME, pointing at the VALUE
*  cell of the LINK just allocated, so it may be assigned through.
-INCLUDE "PUSH.sno"
        PUSH('a')
        PUSH('b')
        PUSH('c')
        OUTPUT  =  TOP()
        OUTPUT  =  POP()
        OUTPUT  =  POP()
        PUSH('z')  =  'ASSIGNED-BY-NAME'
        OUTPUT  =  TOP()
        OUTPUT  =  POP()
        TOP()  =  'TOP-ASSIGNED-BY-NAME'
        OUTPUT  =  POP()
        OUTPUT  =  POP()                        :S(PSH_1)
        OUTPUT  =  'POP ON EMPTY FAILS'
PSH_1   OUTPUT  =  TOP()                        :S(PSH_2)
        OUTPUT  =  'TOP ON EMPTY FAILS'
PSH_2   OUTPUT  =  'DONE'
END
